K5  Up-steps stretch consecutive distances; the Mersenne family
====================================================================================================
  for odd p >= 3:  d(Tp,T^2 p)/d(p,Tp) = 3/2 (p = 3 mod 4) and (3p+1)/(2(p+1)) (p = 1 mod 4)
  (exact, p < 2*10^5); minimum 4/3 at p = 5, supremum 3/2; even steps never stretch.
  x = 2^m - 1 (m = 2..80): T^j x = 3^j 2^(m-j) - 1 (j <= m), so
     d(T^(m-1)x, T^m x) / d(x,Tx) = (3/2)^(m-1)  and  d(x, T^m x)/d(x,Tx) = (3^m - 2^m)/2^(m-1).
