====================================================================================================
F1  Banach in Z_2: every inverse word has exactly one fixed point, the rational periodic point
====================================================================================================
  D(x) = 2x and E(x) = (2x-1)/3 are 2-adic contractions with factor 1/2 (3 is a unit in Z_2); their
  fixed points are 0 and -1.  For every word w of length p <= 12 (all 8190 words):
    the inverse word W has exactly one fixed point in Z_2 (Banach), namely x_w = c_w/(2^p - 3^a);
    Banach iteration from 0 agrees with x_w modulo 2^64 after ceil(64/p)+1 rounds;
    T^p(x_w) = x_w exactly, with parity word w; distinct words give distinct points.
  So Per_p(T) in Z_2 = {Banach fixed points of the 2^p words of length p}: the 'fixed point chain'.

